rationale:
The selected node is the conjunction of three independent book theorems (Simon 7.3.3, 7.4.4, 7.5.8). Their supplied ~50 kB proof shares one toolkit (T1–T10, G), so splitting makes the proof safer and removes threefold duplication.

The parent assembly is exactly ⟨dimred_integer_density_and_tangent_planes, dimred_singular_set_density_below_two, dimred_codimension_one_regularity⟩. The three conjunct children carry the frozen Props unchanged, matching the supplied proof's conclusion ("Parts A, B and C prove … the stated conjunction"). The conditional assembly ⟨A, B, C⟩ typechecks with only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.

The other nine children are reusable obligations, each used by at least two of the conjunct children:
- im_mass_measure;
- zero_dim_vanishing (step 0);
- monotonicity (T1);
- regular_point_density;
- moving_blowups (T2);
- one_dim_cones (T8);
- cone_splitting (T6 + T7 + C3);
- density_gap (G);
- threshold_reduction (T3–T5, T9 with the sibling abstract_dimension_reduction). It is packaged with hypotheses (H1)/(H2), which A discharges with d₀ = n−2, B with d₀ = n−1 and C with d₀ = n−6.

This is v2. The twelve keys, titles, statements, frozen Lean types, lean names and dependencies of v1, all accepted by the audit, are unchanged; they elaborate again and are checked independently. The two required corrections are made.

(R1) Normalization, in threshold_reduction step 3 and integer_density_tangent_planes step 5. Mathlib gives H^n = μHE[n] = c_n·μH[n] with c_n = addHaarScalarFactor ∈ (0, ∞), and μ_A = ϑ_A·H^n. The proofs now state ∫_K ϑ_A dμH[n] = c_n⁻¹·μ_A(K) and the correctly normalized pairings ∫ f·φ_A dμH[n] = c_n⁻¹(∫ f dμ_A)·e₁. So weak convergence of density functions is exactly vague convergence of mass measures, for all currents with locally finite extended mass measure.

(R2) The currentEval-metric assertion is removed from integer_density_tangent_planes 5(d) and from the identical claim in threshold_reduction 2(d). Both now state and prove a countable-test criterion (C) for limits on ℝ^P approximated by currents whose domains exhaust ℝ^P. The criterion rests on uniform local mass bounds valid for every blow-up η_{x',λ'#}T' with |x'| ≤ 1 and λ' ∈ (0, 1]. Step (e) now performs the diagonal selection explicitly and verifies:
- the parameter constraints |x'_k| < 1 − λ'_k;
- eventual support containment, B_{1/λ'_k}(0) ⊆ dom D_k;
- the mass bounds for D_k and for the cone C;
- the test convergence.
The auditor's interval-current obstruction is recorded.

An independent adversarial review of v2 found no blocking defect. Its minor points were applied:
- separate letters s_i and λ_k for defining and tangent scales;
- e₁ for the unit vector of Euclid 1;
- the explicit obstruction example;
- in codimension_one_regularity 5(α) and 5(β)(i), an explicit derivation of |m_y| = 1 from the re-proved mass identity and density 1 of C¹ submanifolds, with 0 ∉ B_{ρ'}(y).

Parts A and C remain large and can be split further at the next depth. As in the accepted parent, White's classification of 2-dimensional minimizing cones and the printed proof of Simons' B.2 are cited inside A and C.
